(@ SYNTAXTABLEENTRY
"(@ CODE \"(@(@ NBSP)eval(@ NBSP)FORM(@ NBSP)...)\") (@ BR)
(@ CODE \"(@(@ NBSP)hide(@ NBSP)FORM(@ NBSP)...)\") (@ BR)
(@ CODE \"(@(@ NBSP)dnl(@ NBSP)FORM(@ NBSP)...)\")"

"(@ TABLERIGHT \"(@ ITAL \\\"Evaluation of\\\")
(@ CODE \\\"FORM(@ NBSP)...\\\") (@ ITAL \\\"as Scheme.\\\")
The “(@ CODE \\\"eval\\\")” version
expands the results, whereas “(@ CODE \\\"hide\\\")” does not. The
“(@ CODE \\\"dnl\\\")” version not only hides the results, it deletes
text up through the next newline.\")"
)

(@ SYNTAXTABLEENTRY
"(@ CODE \"(@(@ NBSP)when(@ NBSP)PREDICATE(@ NBSP)FORM(@ NBSP)...)\") (@ BR)
(@ CODE \"(@(@ NBSP)unless(@ NBSP)PREDICATE(@ NBSP)FORM(@ NBSP)...)\")"

"(@ TABLERIGHT \"(@ ITAL \\\"Deterministic branching.\\\")
For “(@ CODE \\\"when\\\")”, reïnsert the evaluated results of
(@ CODE \\\"FORM(@ NBSP)...\\\")
if (@ CODE \\\"PREDICATE\\\") evaluates as true in Scheme.
For “(@ CODE \\\"unless\\\")”,
reverse the sense of the (@ CODE \\\"PREDICATE\\\").\")"
)

(@ SYNTAXTABLEENTRY
"(@ CODE \"(@(@ NBSP)if(@ NBSP)FORM(@ NBSP)...)\") (@ BR)
(@ CODE \"(@(@ NBSP)while(@ NBSP)FORM(@ NBSP)...)\")"

"(@ TABLERIGHT \"(@ ITAL \\\"Nondeterministic branching and looping.\\\")
The author favors Edsger W. Dijkstra’s nondeterministic branching and
looping. Nondeterminism is by default enforced with a
well seeded random number
generator, to help you catch your errors. The “(@ CODE \\\"if\\\")”
and “(@ CODE \\\"while\\\")” macros do not reïnsert
anything automatically, primarily because otherwise it would
be very difficult to control reïnsertion by “(@ CODE \\\"while\\\")”.
(@ NEWGRAF)If you want the output of (@ CODE \\\"(@(@ NBSP)while(@ NBSP)...)\\\")
expanded recursively, you must use (@ CODE \\\"@in\\\") to
reïnsert iteratively generated parts (@ ITAL \\\"in reverse\\\"). Alternatively,
you can collect the parts into a Scheme structure (such as a string or
string port) and reïnsert them all at once as a string. You could use
a named pipe or other means, too.
(@ NEWGRAF)You can make the branching and looping deterministic
by writing only one (@ CODE \\\"FORM\\\") and putting all the branching logic in
Scheme.\")"
)

(@ SYNTAXTABLEENTRY
"(@ CODE \"(@(@ NBSP)include-raw(@ NBSP)FORM(@ NBSP)...)\") (@ BR)
(@ CODE \"(@(@ NBSP)include(@ NBSP)FORM(@ NBSP)...)\")"

"(@ TABLERIGHT \"(@ ITAL \\\"Inclusion of file contents or command output.\\\")
Include the files specified by (@ CODE \\\"FORM(@ NBSP)...\\\").
The “(@ CODE \\\"include-raw\\\")”
version outputs the file contents verbatim. The “(@ CODE \\\"include\\\")” version
inserts the file contents into the macroprocessing stream.
(@ NEWGRAF)If instead of a filename a (@ CODE \\\"FORM\\\")
 is a string ending in a “(@ VERT)”
character, the inclusion is taken from the output of the shell command
obtained by removing the final “(@ VERT)” character.
This capability is not
present if the (@ CODE \\\"--safer\\\") option is used.\")"
)

(@ SYNTAXTABLEENTRY
"(@ CODE \"(@(@ NBSP)define(@ NBSP)MACRO(@ NBH)NAME(@ NBSP)MACRO(@ NBH)BODY)\") (@ BR)
(@ CODE \"(@(@ NBSP)pushdef(@ NBSP)MACRO(@ NBH)NAME(@ NBSP)MACRO(@ NBH)BODY)\")"

"(@ TABLERIGHT \"(@ ITAL \\\"Macro definition.\\\")
Define a macro with the name given by the form (@ CODE \\\"MACRO(@ NBH)NAME\\\") and
 definition by the form (@ CODE \\\"MACRO(@ NBH)BODY\\\"), which (in the current
implementation) must evaluate to a string. When a macro call is made,
(@ CODE \\\"MACRO(@ NBH)BODY\\\") is inserted and then evaluated recursively. The
“(@ CODE \\\"define\\\")” version pops any top definition of the macro, whereas
“(@ CODE \\\"pushdef\\\")” does not.\")"
)

(@ SYNTAXTABLEENTRY
"(@ CODE \"(@(@ NBSP)popdef(@ NBSP)MACRO(@ NBH)NAME(@ NBSP)...)\")"

"(@ TABLERIGHT \"(@ ITAL \\\"Macro definition pop.\\\")
Remove the most recent macro definition for each given name.\")"
)

(@ SYNTAXTABLEENTRY
"(@ CODE \"(@(@ NBSP)undefine(@ NBSP)MACRO(@ NBH)NAME(@ NBSP)...)\")"

"(@ TABLERIGHT \"(@ ITAL \\\"Macro definition removal.\\\")
Remove all macro definitions corresponding to the given macro names.\")"
)

(@ SYNTAXTABLEENTRY
"(@ CODE \"(@defn(@ NBSP)MACRO(@ NBH)NAME)\")"

"(@ TABLERIGHT \"(@ ITAL \\\"Macro definition retrieval.\\\")
Scheme to return the macro handler for (@ CODE \\\"MACRO(@ NBH)NAME\\\").
This macro
handler can be used as the (@ CODE \\\"MACRO(@ NBH)BODY\\\") for
(@ CODE \\\"(@(@ NBSP)define(@ NBSP)...)\\\") or
(@ CODE \\\"(@(@ NBSP)pushdef(@ NBSP)...)\\\").\")"
)

(@ SYNTAXTABLEENTRY
"(@ CODE \"(@out(@ NBSP)FORM)\") (@ BR)
(@ CODE \"(@out(@ NBSP)FORM(@ NBSP)PORT)\")"

"(@ TABLERIGHT \"(@ ITAL \\\"Outputting text.\\\")
Scheme to try to convert (@ CODE \\\"FORM\\\")
to a string and output the string.\")"
)

(@ SYNTAXTABLEENTRY
"(@ CODE \"(@outs(@ NBSP)FORM)\") (@ BR)
(@ CODE \"(@outs(@ NBSP)FORM(@ NBSP)PORT)\")"

"(@ TABLERIGHT \"(@ ITAL \\\"Outputting an s-expression.\\\")
Scheme to try to convert (@ CODE \\\"FORM\\\")
to an s-expression string and output the string.\")"
)

(@ SYNTAXTABLEENTRY
"(@ CODE \"(@in(@ NBSP)FORM)\")"

"(@ TABLERIGHT \"(@ ITAL \\\"Reïnserting text.\\\")
Scheme to try to convert (@ CODE \\\"FORM\\\")
to a string and prepend the
string to the input (“(@ ITAL \\\"reïnsert\\\")” it).\")"
)

(@ SYNTAXTABLEENTRY
"(@ CODE \"(@ins(@ NBSP)FORM)\")"

"(@ TABLERIGHT \"(@ ITAL \\\"Reïnserting an s-expression.\\\")
Scheme to try to convert (@ CODE \\\"FORM\\\")
to an s-expression string and
prepend the string to the input
(“(@ ITAL \\\"reïnsert\\\")” it).\")"
)

(@ SYNTAXTABLEENTRY
"(@ CODE \"(@raw(@ NBSP)NUMBER)\")"

"(@ TABLERIGHT \"(@ ITAL \\\"Raw outputting of the input.\\\") Scheme
to output (@ CODE \\\"NUMBER\\\") code points from the front of the
input. If there are fewer code points remaining, the entire input is
outputted. All outputted code points are removed from the input.\")" )

(@ SYNTAXTABLEENTRY
"(@ CODE \"(@drop(@ NBSP)NUMBER)\")"

"(@ TABLERIGHT \"(@ ITAL \\\"Skipping some of the input.\\\")
Scheme to drop (@ CODE \\\"NUMBER\\\") code points from the front of the input. If
there are fewer code points remaining, the input is emptied.\")"
)

(@ SYNTAXTABLEENTRY
"(@ CODE \"($a(@ NBSP):=(@ NBSP)(*(@ NBSP)($a)(@ NBSP)(+(@ NBSP)($b)(@ NBSP)1)))\")"

"(@ TABLERIGHT \"(@ ITAL \\\"Imperative variables for use in Scheme.\\\")
The predefined variables are (@ CODE \\\"$a\\\")
to(@ NBSP)(@ CODE \\\"$z\\\") and
(@ CODE \\\"$A\\\") to(@ NBSP)(@ CODE \\\"$Z\\\").\")"
)
